# Secrets
.env
.envrc.local
.envrc.local.d/
# The env-file secrets posture's default file (ADR 1204): plaintext values, never committed.
# Covered by the line above; named so a change to it cannot silently expose the file.
.envrc.local.d/secrets.env
*.pem
*.key

# Internal X.509 CA (ADR 0407 / docs/design/internal-tls-ca.md):
#   - root-cert.pem is PUBLIC distribution material — peers add it as
#     bundle tls_trust_anchor; commit it. The exception overrides the
#     `*.pem` rule above.
#   - ca.key.age is the age-encrypted private signing key — operator-
#     workstation-only; NEVER commit (the *.age suffix is also matched
#     by belt-and-suspenders below).
!ops/enrollment/ca/*/root-cert.pem
# F-090 Path B intermediate cert is also public material (signed by
# the root, no private key inside). Operators install this in their
# macOS keychain to chain-validate every leaf going forward without
# per-leaf trust hacks. Same distribution shape as root-cert.pem.
!ops/enrollment/ca/*/intermediate-cert.pem
# Per-CA-ID raw PUBLIC KEY PEM consumed by wg-cp0-bundle-apply when
# verifying offline-CA-signed bundles on the device side. Public
# material; same distribution shape as the root cert. Each rotation
# adds a new file under public-keys/ with the ca_id in the filename.
# Operators need this checked in so a clean clone can apply bundles
# without first deriving the raw pubkey from the X.509 root.
!ops/enrollment/public-keys/*.pem
# Block 78A-(a) — offline-CA root + intermediate baked into the
# netbird-mgmt container image. Public-material certs committed for
# reproducibility of the image build.
!ops/netbird/ca/root-cert.pem
!ops/netbird/ca/intermediate-cert.pem
ops/enrollment/ca/*/ca.key.age
*.age

# wg-cp0 enrollment operator-laptop state — endpoint+pubkey-only (no
# privkey), but carries the relay-to-mesh mapping + per-device pubkeys
# and shouldn't be in public surface. Operator curates locally; bundles
# rely on these at issuance time but the JSON files don't ride the repo.
# See ops/enrollment/cmd/bundle-create/main.go header for the full
# operator-discipline rationale.
ops/enrollment/wg-cp0-relays.json
ops/enrollment/wg-cp0-relays-prod.json
# wg-cp0-bundle-allowlist.json is promoted to a tracked source-of-truth
# by ADR 0322 / Block 22R.1 — the accessor library at ops/enrollment/peerset
# is now the only path that writes the file, schema v2 is enforced, and
# every change is visible in git history. Per-operator local working
# copies converge through Load → Save round-trips.

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
# Terraform — tree-agnostic, so a NEW terraform-<env>/ tree is covered the day
# it is created rather than the day someone notices. The old form enumerated one
# block per tree, and three of those blocks carried the same comment: "This block
# was missing, so a `terraform init` in the X tree leaked the provider cache into
# git." terraform-zagros-dev, terraform-vega and terraform-govcloud still had no
# block at all, and on 2026-09-08 an init in terraform-zagros-dev staged 743 MB of
# provider cache before it was caught by hand.
#
# .terraform.lock.hcl IS committed (Block 13B supply-chain pin — Terraform
# verifies provider signatures against HashiCorp's signing key using the hashes
# in that file). None of the patterns below match it.
**/.terraform/
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.backup
**/*.tfplan
**/tf.plan
**/crash.log
# operator-local toggle file; the *.example variant IS committed as the template.
**/*.auto.tfvars
!**/*.auto.tfvars.example

# Provisioning
provisioning/.build/

